3. Use above 100,000 MAUs

The grant in Section 2 does not authorize use by an Organization whose
Product exceeds 100,000 MAUs in any calendar month. Before continuing that
use, the Organization must enter into a separate written commercial
agreement with the copyright holder.

The standard commercial pricing basis is an annual fee of US $1 for each
MAU above 100,000. Unless the separate commercial agreement states another
measurement method, the annual fee is calculated as:

  US $1 x (the highest MAU count recorded in any calendar month during the
  Annual License Period minus 100,000), with a minimum result of zero.

For example, if the highest monthly count during an Annual License Period is
125,000 MAUs, the standard annual fee basis is US $25,000.

Payment alone does not create a commercial license. The written commercial
agreement controls the commercial grant, payment schedule, reporting,
support, warranties, and any terms that differ from this license. Contact
the repository owner through https://github.com/RevanthM to request an
agreement before exceeding the threshold.

4. Measurement and records

You are responsible for measuring MAUs in good faith using a reasonable and
consistently applied method. An Organization operating near or above the
threshold must retain sufficient aggregate records to substantiate its MAU
counts for three years. The copyright holder may request a written MAU
certification no more than once per twelve-month period, unless there is a
reasonable basis to suspect a material undercount. No provision of this
license requires collecting personal data that the Product would not
otherwise collect; aggregate, privacy-preserving records are sufficient.

